### t1-rotate
First line k. Then items. Rotate right by k, negative left. m = number of items. k mod m (handle m=0 → print nothing). Right rotation by k: item at new position i = old[(i - k) mod m]. Output lines: for i in 0..m-1 print old[((i - k) mod m + m) mod m].

Compute j = i - k; then j mod m in math sense: ((j % m) + m) % m. Ailullai % follows sign of dividend. So idx = ((j % m) + m) % m.

```
plulai k := plaltai(playadu());
plulai items := [];
plulai line := playadu();
edrushe line <> aiplai
    sutse(items, line);
    line := playadu();
aitudre
plulai m := dra(items);
atdoyal (m > 0) {
    plulai kk := ((k % m) + m) % m;
    shoyo i := 0 busale m - 1
        plulai j := i - kk;
        plulai idx := ((j % m) + m) % m;
        shaibe items[idx];
    pla i
}
```

